WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
We greet you from this place called Pio Casa Colibrí, at this peasant festival in the rural village of El Merojón.

2
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:21.000
He told a woman about the chainsaw: it leaves no trees standing, and now there is no land left here.

3
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Imagine, because peasant culture has something called «picardía» (playful wit).

4
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Where you see it, truly, it was very hard to win over.

5
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:34.000
Back in the village they gave me a few nicknames.

6
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:56.630
[Music and background chatter]

7
00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:58.630
And the other part we did in Bogotá.

8
00:00:58.630 --> 00:01:01.630
Look at how far-reaching this is.

9
00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:06.630
This is done in memory, taking in a bit from an organisation in Brazil.

10
00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:11.630
With a Brazilian foundation that runs the Museum of the Person.

11
00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:16.130
Who can start handing out the texts?

12
00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:24.770
Can you pass them from hand to hand so everyone gets ready?

13
00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:25.770
Stone?

14
00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:26.770
The mountain.

15
00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:27.770
All right, very good.

16
00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:31.770
Well, they did tell me I would get seven women; what they didn't tell me was that they were my wife and six daughters.

17
00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:33.770
All right, very good.

18
00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:42.740
[Peasant guitar music]

19
00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:45.740
Because what one felt here is very beautiful.

20
00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:47.740
I mean, what I felt here.

21
00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:48.740
Thank you very much.

22
00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:51.740
Long live the peasant land!

23
00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:56.000
[Music]

